            <ArticleTitle>Enchondroma as a cause of midfoot pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>139-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Enchondroma is a common bone tumor of the foot. It is often reported in the phalanges and distal metatarsals. The authors, however, present a rare case study of two patients with enchodromas as the cause of midfoot pain. One case presented in the lateral cuneiform which to the authors' knowledge is the first reported case in the literature. Two cases are presented with their surgical management including autogenous calcaneal graft and follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
